# API

One Ninja operation per action (list, detail, create, update). Use a dedicated input schema and output schema, and reuse a schema only when the shape is identical. The endpoint validates, calls `services.<entity>_<action>` or `selectors.<entity>_<action>`, and returns the schema. Import the service module so the endpoint name does not shadow the service. Register the router from `backend/config/api.py`.

New domain code lives in `backend/apps/<name>/` as `models.py`, `services.py`, `selectors.py`, `api.py`, and `schemas.py`.

```python
# ❌ BAD — the import shadows the service, and the endpoint writes
from apps.users.services import user_create

@router.post("/users", response=UserOut)
def user_create(request, payload: UserIn) -> UserOut:
    return User.objects.create(email=payload.email, name=payload.name)

# ✅ GOOD
from apps.users import services

@router.post("/users", response=UserOut)
def user_create(request, payload: UserIn) -> UserOut:
    return services.user_create(email=payload.email, name=payload.name)
```
